          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much protein is in Elevation protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Per the label as reported by reviewers and nutrition databases, Elevation whey gives 30 g of protein per serving at roughly 170 to 180 calories, with about 2 g of sugar. The serving is a large one, about 44 to 49 g of powder, and some tubs describe it as two scoops. Figures vary slightly by flavor and formula version, so check your tub."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Aldi protein powder any good?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is a solid budget whey. The protein comes from whey concentrate and isolate, the same base most supermarket brands use, and buyer reviews generally rate the taste as decent for the price. Its weaknesses are artificial sweeteners, no sport certification and patchy stock. If you need a certified or clean-label powder, look elsewhere; if you want cheap protein, it does the job."
          }
